From: VLCDotNet CI <ci@vlcdotnet>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: robust minimal-set selection and download timeouts

The GitHub Actions runners cannot reach `downloads.videolan.org` (both the
package host and the contrib mirror resolve there), and the default contrib set
pulls ~80 optional third-party archives, many of which only exist on that dead
host. Fetching the whole set therefore stalls for ~130s per unreachable package
before failing.

Two changes make the source-contrib build reliable:

1. Select the build set with `--disable-all --enable-<pkg>`. The stock rule only
   empties the package list when `PKGS_DISABLE` is exactly `all`, but VLC's own
   `extras/package/win32/build.sh` appends extra `--disable-*` flags, so the
   value is never exactly `all` on Windows. Trigger the empty-set path whenever
   `all` appears anywhere in `PKGS_DISABLE`; no real package is named `all`, so
   this is safe and keeps the documented behaviour for the exact-match case.

2. Add `--connect-timeout`/`--retry-delay` to the curl downloader so any
   residual unreachable host fails in seconds instead of stalling the job.

Both hunks were verified to apply cleanly on top of a pristine VLC 3.0.23
checkout after patches 0001-0010.
---
 contrib/src/main.mak | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/contrib/src/main.mak b/contrib/src/main.mak
--- a/contrib/src/main.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/main.mak
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@ endif
 
 ifeq ($(shell curl --version >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo FAIL),)
-download = curl -f -L --retry 3 --output "$@" -- "$(1)"
+download = curl -f -L --connect-timeout 30 --retry 3 --retry-delay 3 --output "$@" -- "$(1)"
 else ifeq ($(shell wget --version >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo FAIL),)
 download = (rm -f $@.tmp && \
 	wget --passive -c -p -O $@.tmp "$(1)" && \
@@ -521,7 +521,7 @@ REQUIRE_GNUV3 = \
 PKGS_FOUND :=
 include $(SRC)/*/rules.mak
 
-ifeq ($(PKGS_DISABLE), all)
+ifneq ($(filter all,$(PKGS_DISABLE)),)
 PKGS :=
 endif
 #
